    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d426">

                <pb facs="0688" n="572" xml:id="pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/4446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-15T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 15,
                                1923—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>250. Your telegram 391, December 9, 2 p.m. Department believes that Sun Yat-sen
                    should not be allowed to seize customhouse at Canton. The plan of the consular
                    body outlined in the telegram from the consul general to the Legation December
                    10, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="84" xml:id="d426-f1"/> is approved.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d426-f1" n="84" xml:id="d426-f1-content">
                <p>See letter from the Secretary of State to President Coolidge, Dec. 13, <ref
                        target="#pg569">p. 569</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
